From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] nmtree: FreeBSD's digest keywords

mtree.h spells the digest keywords that mtree -c writes FreeBSD's way
(md5digest, sha1digest, sha256digest, ripemd160digest) only #ifdef
__FreeBSD__; NeoDarwin's build doesn't define it, so its specifications
said md5, sha1 and sha256, which FreeBSD's mtree reads but doesn't write
(FreeBSD's tests compare against sha256digest: usr.sbin/nmtree/tests).
The keywords are FreeBSD's on Darwin too.

--- a/contrib/mtree/mtree.h	2026-10-05 18:25:41
+++ b/contrib/mtree/mtree.h	2026-10-05 18:25:41
@@ -126,14 +126,14 @@
 void		 free_nodes(NODE *);
 char		*vispath(const char *);
 
-#ifdef __FreeBSD__
+#if defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__APPLE__)
 #define KEY_DIGEST "digest"
 #else
 #define KEY_DIGEST
 #endif
 
 #define	MD5KEY		"md5"		KEY_DIGEST
-#ifdef __FreeBSD__
+#if defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__APPLE__)
 #define	RMD160KEY	"ripemd160"	KEY_DIGEST
 #else
 #define	RMD160KEY	"rmd160"	KEY_DIGEST
